// Title: HackTool - SharpImpersonation Execution
// Sigma ID: f89b08d0-77ad-4728-817b-9b16c5a69c7a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Sai Prashanth Pulisetti @pulisettis, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-27 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1134.001, T1134.003
// Description: Detects execution of the SharpImpersonation tool. Which can be used to manipulate tokens on a
//   Windows computers remotely (PsExec/WmiExec) or interactively
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://s3cur3th1ssh1t.github.io/SharpImpersonation-Introduction/
//   - https://github.com/S3cur3Th1sSh1t/SharpImpersonation
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_sharp_impersonation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\SharpImpersonation.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SharpImpersonation.exe") or ((ProcessCommandLine contains " user:" and ProcessCommandLine contains " binary:") or (ProcessCommandLine contains " user:" and ProcessCommandLine contains " shellcode:") or (ProcessCommandLine contains " technique:CreateProcessAsUserW" or ProcessCommandLine contains " technique:ImpersonateLoggedOnuser"))
